    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8f2b2ed529670b8b84d4d595ec0b3daa4fdb81a79fe5fade57f59c108c864492",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Begin your introduction to Panama City and the Panama Canal with a visit to the Miraflores Locks Visitor Center. Discover the history and operation of the Canal while observing vessels transiting the locks.\n\nContinue to the Biodiversity Museum (Biomuseo), designed by renowned architect Frank Gehry, to discover Panama's extraordinary natural history and biodiversity.\n\nContinue to Casco Viejo, the historic heart of Panama City and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Enjoy lunch before a guided walking tour through its atmospheric streets and historic plazas, discovering colonial and French-influenced architecture, churches and important landmarks.\n\nReturn to the hotel in the afternoon.\n\nOVERNIGHT\n\nPanama City",
